            <ArticleTitle>Recurrent late drug-eluting stent thrombosis upon discontinuation of antiplatelet therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>179-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.carrev.2007.06.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Stent thrombosis is a rare but serious complication of percutaneous coronary intervention. Stent thrombosis usually occurs early after stent implantation but can occasionally occur late, especially when drug-eluting stents are used. We report a case of recurrent late paclitaxel-eluting stent thrombosis (8 and 21 months after initial stent implantation) upon discontinuation of dual antiplatelet therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
